Package: clusterMIO
Title: Sparse Cluster Selection for Linear Mixed Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Madhav", "Shanky", role = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Tom", "Chen", , "tomchen00@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: An L0 (cardinality-constrained) selection of which cluster random
    effects in a linear mixed model are held nonzero, with the rest set to
    exactly zero. The solver profiles out the fixed effects and exploits the
    disjoint support of the one-hot cluster dummies, so each candidate swap has a
    closed-form gain that is independent of the sample size; it depends only on
    'RcppEigen' and needs no commercial optimizer. Provides stability selection
    (Meinshausen-Buhlmann and Shah-Samworth complementary-pairs), an audit-budget
    profile, and a budget-path cluster ranking. Scalable companion to the Julia
    prototype described in arXiv:2302.03157.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppEigen
Imports: Rcpp, stats, utils
Suggests: rpart, lme4, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
URL: https://github.com/MadhavShanky/cluster-mio
